🧠 PWID Care Monitoring System

A frontend-based healthcare monitoring web application designed to support caregivers and healthcare providers working with People with Intellectual Disabilities (PWID).
The system helps in documenting behavior, monitoring physical health, visualizing trends, and assisting caregivers through an intelligent rule-based chatbot.

🎯 Problem Statement

Caregivers and healthcare professionals currently lack a systematic and user-friendly way to:

Record daily behavioral observations

Monitor physical health parameters

Analyze long-term patterns

Identify potential health or behavioral risks early

This project addresses these challenges by providing a centralized monitoring dashboard that works entirely in the browser.

🌟 Key Features
👤 Patient Management

Store basic patient information (name and age)

Data saved securely in browser local storage

🧠 Behavior Tracking

Log daily behavioral observations (Calm, Aggressive, Anxious, etc.)

Maintain historical behavior records

❤️ Physical Health Monitoring

Record weight and body temperature

Track changes over time

📊 Data Visualization

Behavior Frequency Chart (Bar Chart)

Weight Trend Chart (Line Chart)

Temperature Trend Chart (Line Chart)

🤖 Smart Care Assistant (Chatbot)

Rule-based chatbot (no backend, no API)

Understands caregiver queries such as:

Patient summary

Behavior analysis

Health status

Recent records

Generates alerts for:

Repeated aggressive behavior

High temperature

Sudden weight changes

Quick-action buttons for easy interaction

🔐 Privacy & Safety

No internet connection required

No patient data leaves the device

Safe for demo, academic, and prototype use

